WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.600
- We are counting down
to our season two launch.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.650
That's right. Every time.

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:06.850
All right we are counting down

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.650
with uplifting moments from the past year.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.030
Recently we were inspired by the works

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.670
one of our guests was doing to help pets

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:18.010
who, like humans, are very much
in need during the pandemic.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:18.913
Here's a bit of that interview.

00:00:18.913 --> 00:00:20.040
(air swooshing)

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.310
So all those sorts of
animals has inspired you

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.890
to start working with
a new charity, right?

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.360
Tell me what you're doing.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.010
- Yeah. So there's this charity
called Stay Home and Foster

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.630
and you know, they've already
been doing a great job

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.210
of trying to get people to foster animals

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:37.270
and with Stay Home and Foster,

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.290
we are actually doing
this next phase of it now,

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.030
which I'm really excited about,

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.853
which is called Fido
Foster or Feline Foster.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:50.450
And basically we're trying
to create a community

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.670
that connects all the
shelters in our country

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:56.620
and be one place that people can go to.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:59.540
And it's also somewhere that goes beyond

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.960
just giving you the dog, you know,

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.020
you can go on and say like,

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:04.930
what are the things that we
shouldn't be giving our dogs

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.520
and what are the things
we should be giving them?

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.520
So, yeah so with Fido and Feline Foster,

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.560
we are trying to create
a real strong community,

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.120
that will last, you know,

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.680
and that is somewhere
that everybody can trust

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.520
and go and be able to
help save these animals

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.630
and, you know, and add
a little furry friend

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.920
to their family.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.730
- All right. Well, now she's
back to update us on her work

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:29.120
with Wag and the Fido Foster organization.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.260
She is helping our
furry friends everywhere

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:32.580
and we love her for it.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.650
And for many reasons,
she's just fun as hell.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.620
Olivia Munn, everybody.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:38.115
Hello? (laughs)

00:01:38.115 --> 00:01:40.360
- What are you, are you
wearing a NASA suit?

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.460
- I am wearing a space suit, Olivia,

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:44.820
'cause we're really clever at this show

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.560
and we're launching season two.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.470
I came with a helmet
and everything. (laughs)

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.490
- I love it.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.600
- I basically high don't
get embarrassed at anything.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.610
So anything anyone asks me to do,

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:02.150
I generally just say yes and
jump right in the deep end.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:04.490
So I feel like--

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.760
- If you had given me a suit,
I would have worn it too.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.370
- I know. I feel like we're
similar in that sense.

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:10.203
- Yeah.

00:02:10.203 --> 00:02:12.960
- First I need an update on
your mom's online shopping.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.600
So what's been the latest
purchase she's made you make.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.633
- Well, the latest purchase
was, so back for father's day.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.500
My mom said that my stepfather, Sam

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.440
wanted a hammock because
we're in quarantine.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.390
They can't be beyond, they
have a big beautiful yard,

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:31.890
called her gardening around.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:35.140
And so I said, great,
I'll get you guys two

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.500
so you guys can enjoy together.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.560
And then the other day
I thought to ask my mom,

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.290
you know, how's the hammock life going?

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:44.440
She's like, "It's really good."

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.340
And I said, what about Sam?

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:46.627
How's it going? And he said,

00:02:46.627 --> 00:02:48.967
"Oh, I'm not using it" and my mum said,

00:02:48.967 --> 00:02:52.793
"Yeah, no, no. I put the other
one into the storage unit"

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.920
and I was like, well, why Sam wants one?

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.320
She's like, "No, no, one's for me.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.610
And one's for me for later."

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:03.750
So I was like, so then
Sam's, father said get this,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.200
she picked out for him
that was from the children

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.720
was really just for her,

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.520
which is very not surprising.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:14.110
- Which is just a lie. That's awesome.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:17.468
Well, what is the latest
with Fido foster organization

00:03:17.468 --> 00:03:18.301
that you're part of?

00:03:18.301 --> 00:03:19.220
You were talking about that last time.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.650
- Yeah. Well, it's been
doing really great.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:25.740
And the thing that we've really been proud

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.760
about incorporating is
training for people.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.450
So, you know, I've worked with Wag

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:32.580
and we've done a lot of stuff with Wag

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.110
when it comes to like a dog sitting,

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.710
boarding, walking your dog,

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:39.420
but then we've added this new thing

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:40.980
to help people train their dogs

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:44.110
and they can do these
one-on-ones with trainers online,

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.860
like these 30 minute training sessions,

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.910
which is super important because
when we started doing this

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.950
Stay Home and Foster at the
beginning of quarantine,

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:53.010
Wag and I helped with
Stay Home and Foster,

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:56.470
and we really wanted people
to be able to, you know,

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:57.810
hopefully adopt these dogs

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.280
and we take them into their lives.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.890
And I know having pets and you do as well.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.920
Like the training that they go through,

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.790
if you can get any little bit of training

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:09.570
helps make your life and
their life so much better.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:11.490
So it was something that I always pushed

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:12.930
in the beginning of working with Wag.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:16.720
And now we've found out
this amazing process,

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:18.660
especially with online
and doing things virtually

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:19.570
that people can sign up

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.620
and actually work with a dog trainer.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.460
So we've been doing that and helping that

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:26.100
and offering that to people
which has been really exciting

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:29.250
to see like people learning
how to train their dogs better.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.510
And then, you know, these
dogs like flourishing

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:34.400
and these new families,
it's been really exciting.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.920
- Absolutely.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.840
All right. Well, I love
hanging out with you so much,

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.480
Olivia. I think you are so cool.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.290
Thank you for stopping by.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:44.770
Everybody be sure to check
out Wag for dog training tips

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:47.290
and also go online to find
out how you can help more

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:49.353
with the Fido Foster Organization cause.

